  - id: song_of_zions_joy
    displayName: Song of Zion's Joy
    flavorText: The LORD promises to dwell in the midst of a humbled, restored Zion,
      rejoicing over her with singing and gathering her scattered exiles home.
    tierType: 1
    purpose: Closes the book by reversing its own opening judgment, promising Judah
      a pure language to call on the LORD together, a humble surviving remnant that
      will not do iniquity or speak lies, and the LORD himself dwelling in the midst
      of Zion, rejoicing over her with singing, before gathering the scattered home
      and turning their captivity.
